hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer a question from one of  my Facebook reader Syed who wants to  start a new ice cream business and  wanted my advice on how to get started  and we had a couple questions so  specifically is asking about Facebook  how to advertise on Facebook if it's  worth setting up a website or a brand  page on Facebook what do I think about  partnering up with shops or creating the  shop in a university college or shopping  mall and how do you promote the the  company so thanks to the questions I had  I think it's a very common question a  lot of entrepreneurs face when they're  starting a new business and so hopefully  we can answer questions that a lot of  entrepreneurs are facing right now in  terms of the Facebook thing I think it's  a good idea to have a Facebook page for  your company it's really easy to set up  you don't need to have a lot of  technical skills and a lot of  entrepreneurs are using that instead of  having their own website just because  it's so easy to set up and they can  manage everything themselves that may  not be an ideal kind of long-term  situation but a lot of entrepreneurs  will launch with just a Facebook page  and then as you're making money you're  able to afford going out and getting a  designer and creating your own website  I'm a big believer in not spending a lot  of money until I'm making money so this  is a great way to do it if you just  create a Facebook page doesn't cost you  anything you make a quick banner and you  start promoting your business before you  actually go up launch your site now in  terms of the Facebook ads that can be  really tough because it's really hard to  make direct sales to Facebook ads the  Facebook community is more about  building relationships and getting  people interested in what you're doing  and then hopefully after they've you  know built that relationship with you  they end up buying whatever product or  service you're having but for you know  just to advertise your ice cream product  you're probably not going to make a lot  of money off of Facebook Ads directly  your better bet is to promote your page  have a lot of great content have some  fun things that make people want to come  back and of course also promote your ice  cream products and so it's a longer term  commitment with anything else I like  testing things so try it out see if it  works you know commit a minimum or  maximum budget I guess to it and see if  your  optimal with that so you can say 100  bucks 200 bucks 500 bucks dude if you're  comfortable with but don't go you know  too far beyond because it's easy to to  spend a lot of money right anybody can  spend money and I want to make sure  you're you're the entrepreneur can  actually make money doing this I think  with any new entrepreneur venture it's  really important to test on a small  scale to see if what you have is a  really good idea or not I don't know why  I chose the ice cream business hopefully  it's because you have a strong passion  for ice cream and you think you can  really make a go out of it in it and  it's not just something to try and make  a lot of money  we recently post on our website at a  profile of Ben &amp; Jerry's from there the  ice cream Ben and Jerry and they started  from a five dollar ice cream making  corpse and they launched out of an old  gas station so I might be an  inspirational story for you to read but  I think for you to get started what I  would try to do is partner up I think  that's your best bet right now be able  to see if it works and start getting  access to potential customers so I don't  the idea is that you mentioned I think  your best bet would be to try to get  into the universities colleges shopping  malls but don't do it by getting your  own stall that can be really expensive  and you're blowing again a lot of money  and you don't know if it's going to work  out or not what I would try to do is  partner up with somebody who's already  there and try to get a portion of their  table maybe for a day a week month  weekends whatever it is whenever you  think you know you would probably get  some customers coming in partner up with  them you can either give them ideally  just a cut of the revenue but you may  have to give them a set fee but it's  going to be a lot cheaper to do that on  a one offer or two off or three offers  you test it then to try to get your own  booth for a month or quarter or year  it's going to be really expensive so  that way you can test it see if that  market works to you or not and if it  does then you can say hey this makes  sense for me to get my own booth and if  it doesn't then you haven't wasted a lot  of money needlessly so it's really  important to test on a small scale so  you'll find somebody who is also selling  to those markets see if you can strike  up some kind of partnership and from  there you will discover if that is your  target market or not and if people are  willing to buy your ice cream products  right so good luck and hopefully that  answer some of your questions for you  because as you're watching if you liked  the video please give it a thumbs up  below it makes you want to do more of  these videos for you guys  and if you have a question that I can  answer for your business or a comment  about the video feel free to leave it in  the comments below I always read those  and try to respond to as many as it can  so thank you and you'll see you on the  next episode  you  you
 

